research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-gauge.md-76-| **def-qftx-bv-antibracket-master-action** | definition / mathematics | Specify field/antifield degrees, parities, the odd symplectic antibracket and its sign convention, minimal/nonminimal sectors, and the classical master action for the declared irreducible Yang–Mills model. State which infinite-dimensional/formal operations are used. |
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-gauge.md-77-| **lem-qftx-bv-master-equation-brst-nilpotence** | lemma / mathematics | Prove from the chosen antibracket Jacobi identity that the Hamiltonian differential \(s=(S_{\mathrm{BV}},-)\) squares to zero exactly when the classical master equation holds. Do not infer a measure or the quantum master equation from the classical one. |
