items/def-csm-frontier-bernoulli-relative-free-energy.md:40:For $u\in(0,1)$ define the Bernoulli free-energy density $f(u):=u\log u+(1-u)\log(1-u)$. For a reference density $\bar\rho\in(0,1)$ define $h(u\mid\bar\rho):=f(u)-f(\bar\rho)-\bigl(\log\bar\rho-\log(1-\bar\rho)\bigr)(u-\bar\rho)$. For $d\ge1$, a smooth profile $\rho:\mathbb T^d\to[\varepsilon,1-\varepsilon]$ with some $0<\varepsilon<1/2$, and normalized product Haar measure $dx$ on $\mathbb T^d$, define $\mathcal H_{\bar\rho}(\rho):=\int_{\mathbb T^d}h(\rho(x)\mid\bar\rho)\,dx$. If $\int_{\mathbb T^d}\rho\,dx=\bar\rho$, then $\mathcal H_{\bar\rho}(\rho)=\int_{\mathbb T^d}f(\rho(x))\,dx-f(\bar\rho)$ because the linear term integrates to zero. All logarithm arguments are positive on the stated domains.
