## Example

Take (N_s=N_t=3), (a>0), and (g_0>0) in the adopted pure SU(2) Euclidean Wilson regulator. Let (C) be the elementary spatial plaquette at the origin in the ((1,2))-plane at (t=0), and set (W_C(u)=\tfrac12\operatorname{ReTr}_2(U_C)). At the configuration with every link matrix equal to (I_2), the Wilson action is zero and (W_C=1). For every link configuration, (W_C) is a bounded gauge-invariant multiplication observable. Its normalized finite-volume expectation exists; the one-step transfer operator is bounded and maps the group-invariant Gauss sector into itself, which contains the nonzero constant wavefunction; and cyclic iteration of its kernel reproduces the finite periodic Euclidean integral. These are exact finite-regulator statements; they assert no continuum area law or Lorentzian energy spectrum.

