@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+# Batch 22 — Compact Non-Abelian Finite-Lattice Regulator
+
+## Plan and design comparison
+
+The complete assigned design section at plan-track lines 303–315 matches the current canonical plan rows: A page qftx-nonabelian-lattice-regulator, B page qftx-nonabelian-lattice-regulator-examples, title, category, physics library, order 978, and required A-page supplier qftx-nonabelian-lattice-mathematics all agree. Its scope is a finite compact-G regulator with exact finite-volume observables, a physical slice sector and a transfer/Hamiltonian convention, with no continuum-limit claim. No A/B identity, placement, title, order, or page-prerequisite conflict was found.
+
+The candidate postulate contract in proposed-inventory.json is post-qftx-nonabelian-lattice-regulator. The specialist note explicitly rejects extending the compact U(1) rotor model by relabeling U(1) as non-Abelian G. The authored postulate therefore adopts a pure SU(2) Wilson model directly, uses its defining trace, and includes no dynamical matter. It makes no confinement, matter-screening, Hamiltonian-spectrum, or continuum claim.
+
+The proposed postulate contract lists no item-level dependencies, but exact lattice variables, vertex action, plaquette product, normalized Haar measure, and Gauss-sector convention are necessary formulation inputs. The postulate records the planned item def-qftx-nonabelian-lattice-gauge-data as a formulation prerequisite and also restates the required interface in its complete Statement. This new direct item edge is recorded open; no shared plan was edited.
+
+The A page also gains lem-qftx-su2-compact-nonabelian-group, a local mathematical supplier needed to instantiate compact non-Abelian SU(2) without importing a broader Lie-geometry assumption. The proof uses the published choice-free Heine–Borel result and finite matrix algebra. Supplier-first item levels are: SU(2) lemma 0; postulate 1, from the level-0 planned lattice-data item and local lemma; B-page example 2, from the level-1 postulate. The run's full batch input remains batch 22 at level 2, requiring batch 6.
+
+## Prerequisite and readiness audit
+
+- The complete current carrier items/thm-heine-borel-rn.md was inspected. It proves closed-and-bounded compactness in finite-dimensional Euclidean space by choice-free bisection. No AC or AC_omega is used in the local SU(2) group proof.
+- The exact planned batch-6 data interface is the proposed def-qftx-nonabelian-lattice-gauge-data contract in the integrated inventory: finite oriented lattice/complex; compact-G edge variables; vertex gauge action; plaquette product; Haar product measure or Hamiltonian link Hilbert space; Gauss generators; all conventions. Its current batch-6 manifest still has empty A/B item arrays, and the local item and page carriers are absent.
+- Before deciding readiness, loadStep1Record and step1Decision were called for def-qftx-nonabelian-lattice-gauge-data. At that audit the item had no run ownership, was not in the canonical active item map, and its current Step-1 record was missing. This is a real absent carrier/readiness input, not a blocker inferred from draft status, pending precheck, or independent approval.
+- The normalized-Haar input is sourced from the current published cor-normalized-haar-probability-on-a-compact-group and def-axiom-of-choice. Their exact statements and complete proofs were inspected. Full AC is required only by the imported compact-group Haar-existence theorem; it is declared in the postulate, included in deps, and carried directly by the B example. The local SU(2) compactness lemma itself is choice-free.
+- The batch-6 A page transitively requires qftx-gauge-geometry (batch 2). Its current page and item inventory were inspected. The finite-lattice-data candidate has no item-level dependency on the principal-connection statements, and this regulator uses no principal connection, bundle curvature, or associated connection. Therefore the AC_omega hypothesis in that separate connection chain is not imported here. The transitive page observation is recorded in these notes, not as a batch-22-owned cross-batch row.
+- Published compact U(1) rotor/CAR items on qft-g02 were checked as boundary context only. They are not dependencies and do not supply SU(2) variables, Wilson plaquettes, or the non-Abelian slice sector.
+
+## Source reading and disposition
+
+Two independent full treatments were read: Michael Creutz's open-access textbook Quarks, Gluons and Lattices and David Tong's full lecture-note chapter Lattice Gauge Theory. Exact URLs, locators, read extents, supported item IDs, limitations, and included dispositions are listed in batch-22.coverage.json.
+
+- Creutz Chapter 7, pp. 34–38: directed group-valued links and inverses; plaquette Wilson action; compact-group integration; exact finite-cutoff gauge symmetry.
+- Creutz Chapter 8, pp. 39–43: invariant integration on compact groups, normalized left/right invariance, and SU(2) parametrization.
+- Creutz Chapter 15, pp. 101–107: Wilson transfer construction, slice L²(G) convention, residual vertex transformations, and the group-singlet Gauss sector. The authored postulate uses only a finite Euclidean transfer kernel and does not take the time-continuum Hamiltonian limit.
+- Tong Chapter 4, §§4.2.1–4.2.3, printed pp. 206–215: link variables and gauge transformations, Wilson action, normalized Haar product, finite Euclidean observables, and the strong-coupling discussion's separation from continuum claims.
+- Retrieval history: a Kogut 1979 review PDF mirror at https://scalettar.physics.ucdavis.edu/p219a/RevModPhys.51.659.pdf returned HTTP 502 when opened. Searches then located the full Creutz textbook chapters and Tong lecture-note chapter; both independent treatments were retrieved and inspected. Kogut was not selected as an item source, and no claim is attributed to its failed mirror.
+
+## Authored items and exact use
+
+- lem-qftx-su2-compact-nonabelian-group proves group closure, closedness and boundedness in R^8, compactness by thm-heine-borel-rn, Hausdorffness from its inherited metric, and non-Abelianness by explicit matrices.
+- post-qftx-nonabelian-lattice-regulator adopts the finite periodic Euclidean SU(2) Wilson model. It specifies the global matrix group, units, lattice sizes, link and plaquette conventions, vertex gauge action, normalized Haar product measure, action, finite-volume expectation, group-invariant slice sector, and transfer kernel. AC appears only for normalized Haar existence. No dynamical matter, continuum, infinite-volume, confinement, or Lorentzian Hamiltonian statement is made.
+- ex-qftx-su2-wilson-lattice-transfer-sector conditionally verifies Wilson-loop gauge invariance and boundedness, positive finite partition function, bounded transfer operator, invariance and nonemptiness of the Gauss sector, and cyclic transfer-kernel factorization.
+- Direct batch-22 cross-batch rows are exactly the A-page requirement on qftx-nonabelian-lattice-mathematics and the postulate's planned data-definition edge. Both remain open until the actual batch-6 carriers are available and checked. The B page's A-page edge is within batch 22.
+
